From: MinGit BusyBox Bundle maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] win32: preserve Unicode paths and inherited shell values

Based on git-for-windows/busybox-w32
 d8d8bb397f1e200ba5a871dc6aa4af819b23f32a.
Upstream BusyBox-w32 is maintained by Ron Yorston, originally ported by
Nguyễn Thái Ngọc Duy; Git for Windows carries additional downstream changes.
Source: https://github.com/git-for-windows/busybox-w32
Upstream: https://github.com/rmyorston/busybox-w32
Bundle integration changes: GPL-2.0-only; upstream attribution is unchanged.

CI 41929624612 showed identical executable bytes and Windows owner/SDDL
producing mode 755 for an ASCII filename but 750 for its Chinese sibling.
Reuse the already converted wpath with CreateFileW for READ_CONTROL, keeping
all owner checks, reparse handling and failure behavior. CI 41934339387 then
passed nonadministrator Unicode-path local clone and ls-remote.

That run also captured UTF-8 shell PATH becoming mojibake in a native child,
and backslash escapes in GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS becoming forward slashes.
Use upstream's UTF-8 manifest mode, with an explicit Windows 10 1903+ floor
and rejection when unsupported. Keep all other mingw64_defconfig features,
including the existing TLS backend and permission metadata. Preserve the
UCRT NULL-environment workaround rather than reintroducing upstream #234.

Default the existing winxp option on so imported values remain opaque.
This is a path-conversion option, not Windows XP platform support. Explicit
+X remains available. No Git-specific environment-variable exception is used.
Upstream option/manifest rationale:
https://frippery.org/busybox/release-notes/FRP-5181.html
The real Unicode-path clone, nested alias, hook and LFS gates remain required.
---

diff --git a/configs/mingw64_defconfig b/configs/mingw64_defconfig
index 97aac7f..d09968c 100644
--- a/configs/mingw64_defconfig
+++ b/configs/mingw64_defconfig
@@ -48,9 +48,9 @@ CONFIG_GLOBBING=y
 CONFIG_FEATURE_RESOURCES=y
 CONFIG_FEATURE_VERSIONINFO=y
 # CONFIG_FEATURE_TOOLCHAIN_MANIFEST is not set
-CONFIG_FEATURE_APP_MANIFEST=y
-# CONFIG_FEATURE_UTF8_MANIFEST is not set
-# CONFIG_FEATURE_FAIL_IF_UTF8_MANIFEST_UNSUPPORTED is not set
+# CONFIG_FEATURE_APP_MANIFEST is not set
+CONFIG_FEATURE_UTF8_MANIFEST=y
+CONFIG_FEATURE_FAIL_IF_UTF8_MANIFEST_UNSUPPORTED=y
 CONFIG_FEATURE_ICON=y
 # CONFIG_FEATURE_ICON_ATERM is not set
 # CONFIG_FEATURE_ICON_STERM is not set
diff --git a/shell/ash.c b/shell/ash.c
index 7fb5af8..cdb0b7d 100644
--- a/shell/ash.c
+++ b/shell/ash.c
@@ -16574,6 +16574,11 @@ procargs(char **xargv)
 	argptr = xargv;
 	for (i = 0; i < NOPTS; i++)
 		optlist[i] = 2;
+#if ENABLE_PLATFORM_MINGW32
+	/* Preserve opaque inherited values, including native command escapes.
+	 * Users may still request slash conversion explicitly with +X. */
+	winxp = 1;
+#endif
 	if (options(&login_sh)) {
 		/* it already printed err message */
 		raise_exception(EXERROR); /* does not return */
diff --git a/win32/mingw.c b/win32/mingw.c
index aaf041e..abad6f2 100644
--- a/win32/mingw.c
+++ b/win32/mingw.c
@@ -1113,7 +1113,7 @@ static int do_lstat(int follow, const char *file_name, struct mingw_stat *buf)
 			flags = FILE_FLAG_BACKUP_SEMANTICS;
 			if (S_ISLNK(buf->st_mode))
 				flags |= FILE_FLAG_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT;
-			fh = CreateFile(file_name, READ_CONTROL, 0, NULL,
+			fh = CreateFileW(wpath, READ_CONTROL, 0, NULL,
 								OPEN_EXISTING, flags, NULL);
 			if (fh != INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE) {
 				if (GetFileInformationByHandle(fh, &hdata)) {
